1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,130
Why can hot water crack a frozen

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:02,830
windshield?

3
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:05,000
One splash from the kettle...

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,300
and the glass can split right across.

5
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:08,940
Glass is slow to move heat.

6
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:11,360
So the outer layer warms and swells in

7
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,220
a second, while the glass underneath is

8
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,020
still frozen.

9
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,360
One side stretching, the other side not.

10
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:18,470
That pull is called thermal shock.

11
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:20,090
A tiny chip makes it worse.

12
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:22,450
The stress gathers there, and a crack can

13
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:23,820
race across the glass.

14
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:25,170
So skip the kettle.

15
00:00:25,590 --> 00:00:27,690
Scrape it, spray de-icer, or let the

16
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:28,890
defroster warm it slowly...

17
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:30,570
and the ice slides right off.
